---
// src/pages/services/washer-repair/ge-error-codes.astro
// Info Wave W4 — GE washer error codes (brand umbrella sniper, HONEST-THIN).
// Angle: GE mostly shows plain-language messages, not cryptic codes. Few real numeric codes.
// Honest callout: E10/E20/E40/E60/E90 are Electrolux/Frigidaire, NOT GE (charts mislabel them).
// Newer UltraFast combo uses numeric codes (model-specific; read on-site, no invented meanings).
// Older Profile E1-E28 = tech. Codes verified vs GE Appliances support. $89 residential. 4 schema entities.
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, toE164 } from '../../../data/branches';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../../lib/build-location-array';

const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/services/washer-repair/ge-error-codes/";

const title = "GE Washer Error Codes? Causes & Fix — Same Day";
const description = `GE washer showing a message or code? GE mostly speaks in plain words, not cryptic codes. What's real and what's mislabeled Electrolux. $89 diagnostic.`;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why can't I find a GE washer error-code chart like LG or Samsung has?",
    a: "Because GE mostly doesn't use cryptic codes — it uses plain-language messages. Where an LG shows OE and a Samsung shows 5C, a GE washer typically prints something readable like 'Confirm Water Supply,' 'Check and Clean Drain Pump Filter,' or lights a spin/unbalance indicator. That's not a gap in the documentation; it's a design choice. So if you're hunting for a big GE code table, there mostly isn't one, and that's fine — the machine already told you the category in words. We diagnose GE by reading that message plus on-site testing. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "I found a GE chart online with E10, E20, E40, E60 codes. Are those real GE codes?",
    a: "No — and this is a common mix-up. E10, E20, E40, E60, E70, and E90 are Electrolux and Frigidaire codes, not GE. A lot of aggregated 'error code' sites lump brands together and mislabel that E-series as GE. If your washer is actually showing E20 or E40, check the badge: it's very likely a Frigidaire or Electrolux machine, in which case our Frigidaire/Electrolux section on the main washer error-codes page has the right table. GE genuinely doesn't use that E10/E20/E40 scheme."
  },
  {
    q: "My GE washer says 'Check and Clean Drain Pump Filter' or won't drain. What do I do?",
    a: "That message means a drain fault, same category as an LG OE or a Whirlpool F9E1. On GE front-load models with an accessible filter, that's the first stop: small lower-front access door, pan underneath, twist the cap, clear the lint and coins. If GE didn't put a customer filter on your model, the drain path runs to the pump and hose, which is a technician check. When it's the drain pump motor, replacement runs $380 to $540. Our washer not-draining page walks the whole path."
  },
  {
    q: "'Confirm Water Supply' or the washer won't fill — what's wrong?",
    a: "That's a fill/water-supply message, GE's plain-language version of a Samsung 4C or LG IE. Work cheap to expensive: both supply valves fully open, fill hoses not kinked behind the machine, then the mesh inlet screens where the hoses thread on (sediment clogs those in our harder-water areas). If the inlet valve solenoid itself failed, that's a $260 to $380 replacement. A large share of these clear at the hose or screen without a part."
  },
  {
    q: "The spin light is flashing or it says the load is unbalanced. Is that a fault?",
    a: "Usually not, at first. GE flags an unbalanced load with a spin indicator or a plain message when the drum can't safely ramp to spin speed off-center. On one lopsided load (a single comforter, towels bunched to one side) it's the machine protecting itself — spread the load and it spins. If it flags unbalance on balanced loads too, then we look at worn suspension or a balance sensor, which is a $440 to $640 repair. So the first move is genuinely just to redistribute the wash."
  },
  {
    q: "My GE UltraFast combo shows a numeric code. Is that different from a regular GE washer?",
    a: "Yes. The newer GE UltraFast washer/dryer combo does use numeric fault codes, and those are specific to that combo unit — they don't map to the plain-language messages on GE's standalone washers. Because those codes shift by model and firmware, we don't reproduce a chart that might not match your exact unit; instead our techs read the code off your machine, cross-reference GE's current service documentation for that model, and diagnose from there. If you have an UltraFast combo throwing a code, tell us the number when you call and we'll come prepared."
  },
  {
    q: "Older GE Profile washer showing an 'E' code with a number — what is that?",
    a: "Older GE Profile front-loaders used an E-series (roughly E1 through the E20s) for motor, control, and sensor faults — a different scheme from both today's plain-language GE and from the Electrolux E-codes people confuse them with. Those older Profile codes are technician-level: they point at the motor, the control board, or a sensor, and the diagnosis needs a meter. If you have an aging Profile flashing an E-number, it's worth a service call rather than a DIY reset, and at that age we'll also give you the honest repair-versus-replace read."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I reset a GE washer?",
    a: "Unplug for about 60 seconds (or flip the breaker), restore power, and run a short cycle to see if the message returns. For most plain-language messages, fixing the underlying cause (open the valve, clear the filter, redistribute the load) clears the message on its own. GE washers don't need a special reset dance for customer-side issues. If a message returns immediately after you've addressed the obvious cause, that's a real hardware fault and worth a visit."
  },
  {
    q: "Is a GE washer worth repairing, or should I replace it?",
    a: "Depends on age and the failing part. A GE washer in its first 6 to 8 years with a single failure — a drain pump, an inlet valve, a lock — is almost always worth repairing; those are bounded parts. Once a machine is year 10-plus and starts stacking failures, we give you the honest math at the door: what the specific repair costs against a comparable new unit. We'd rather tell you to replace a tired machine than sell you a part it doesn't make sense to buy. $89 diagnostic, waived if you go ahead with the repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty?",
    a: "90 days on SDAR labor and parts for the work we perform — separate from any GE factory warranty. Same component fails inside 90 days, we replace it free. BHGS #A49573, BBB Accredited Business, EPA 608 Universal certified #1346255700410. $89 residential diagnostic, waived when you approve the repair."
  }
];

const schemaJsons = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "address": { "@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "West Hollywood", "addressRegion": "CA", "addressCountry": "US" },
    "@id": canonical + "#business",
    "name": "Same Day Appliance Repair",
    "url": canonical,
    "telephone": toE164(phone),
    "priceRange": "$$",
    "openingHoursSpecification": [
        { "@type": "OpeningHoursSpecification", "dayOfWeek": ["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday","Saturday"], "opens": "08:00", "closes": "20:00" },
        { "@type": "OpeningHoursSpecification", "dayOfWeek": "Sunday", "opens": "00:00", "closes": "00:00" }
      ],
    "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ],
    "legalName": "HVAC 777 LLC",
    "hasCredential": [ { "@type": "EducationalOccupationalCredential", "credentialCategory": "BHGS Registration #A49573", "recognizedBy": { "@type": "GovernmentOrganization", "name": "California Bureau of Household Goods and Services" } }, { "@type": "EducationalOccupationalCredential", "credentialCategory": "EPA 608 Universal Certification #1346255700410", "recognizedBy": { "@type": "GovernmentOrganization", "name": "U.S. Environmental Protection Agency" } }, { "@type": "EducationalOccupationalCredential", "credentialCategory": "CSLB C-20 HVAC", "recognizedBy": { "@type": "GovernmentOrganization", "name": "California Contractors State License Board" } }, { "@type": "EducationalOccupationalCredential", "credentialCategory": "BBB Accredited Business", "recognizedBy": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Better Business Bureau" } } ],
  "location": BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL

  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "@id": canonical + "#service",
    "serviceType": "GE Washer Error Code Repair",
    "name": "GE Washer Error Code and Message Diagnostic and Repair Service",
    "url": canonical,
    "description": "Residential GE washer diagnostic and repair across all seven Southern California counties. GE washers mostly display plain-language messages (Confirm Water Supply, Check and Clean Drain Pump Filter, unbalanced-load indicator) rather than cryptic codes. Newer GE UltraFast combo units use model-specific numeric codes; older GE Profile front-loaders use an E-series (technician). Note: E10/E20/E40/E60/E90 are Electrolux/Frigidaire codes, not GE. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified #1346255700410.",
    "provider": { "@id": canonical + "#business" },
    "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ],
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "priceSpecification": { "@type": "PriceSpecification", "price": "89.00", "priceCurrency": "USD", "description": "Residential diagnostic fee, waived with repair" } }
  },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a } })) },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/services/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Washer Repair", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/services/washer-repair/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "name": "GE Error Codes", "item": canonical }
    ]
  }
];
